From a7d2869a72f56635a71ac8ab4669f23c8bfa3ff6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(complete): Support flag subcommands in native
 completions

Pacman-style subcommands (`Command::short_flag`, `Command::long_flag`) were
neither offered nor followed, so `-S <TAB>` completed the parent command.

Now `-S`/`--sync` (and their aliases) are offered with the other flags and
switch completions to the subcommand.
Like the parser, a short flag subcommand can appear anywhere in a group of
short flags (`-vSs`), with the remaining flags belonging to the subcommand.
As they share an id with the subcommand name, they are not repeated when
the name is already offered, e.g. for an empty argument.
